  "final_message": "Done. Built and verified the full stack.\n\n## What I implemented\n\n**Backend** (`backend/app.py`) \u2014 Flask + SQLite (WAL) under `./data`:\n- Register (201), login (200 + bearer token), `GET /api/me`, `GET /api/me/login-attempts`\n- Lockout: 5 consecutive failures \u2192 429 for 15 min (even with correct password); success resets counter; expired locks clear automatically\n- Per-client rate limit: 20 attempts/60s \u2192 429; both 429s include `Retry-After`\n- Admin account seeded from `ADMIN_PASSWORD` at startup (disabled/removed when unset); admin-only lock listing + unlock endpoints\n- Serves the built frontend with SPA fallback; `GET /api/health` \u2192 `{\"status\":\"ok\"}`\n\n**Frontend** (`frontend/src`) \u2014 React + TypeScript + Tailwind v4:\n- Register/sign-in tabs, signed-in username + sign-out\n- Lockout/rate-limit messages with live \"try again in \u2026\" countdown\n- Account page: last sign-in + 20 recent attempts (success/failed badges)\n- Admin page: locked usernames with unlock button (auto-refresh)\n\n**Notes:**\n- Removed `backend/requirements.lock` \u2014 it enabled pip hash-checking mode that would fail the Docker build (README permits removing it).\n- Added Tailwind, TypeScript, and React type packages; created `tsconfig.json`, `index.css`, `.gitignore`.\n- Verified with the Flask test client (lockout, rate limit, reset, unlock, persistence across restart, admin gating) and confirmed `tsc --noEmit` plus `npm run build` succeed. Docker isn't installed here, but gunicorn startup and static/API serving were tested directly.",
  "final_message_truncated": false,
